Z||000004||Spektyr||05-11-2001||07:43 AM||||Interesting car... it's kinda like that color-changing paint.<P>It's an RX7 from the front, a Testarossa from the side, and Corvette from the back.<P>One of a kind?  Yeah.  The only way this thing would've seen production is in a joint venture by Mazda, Chevy, and Ferrari.<P>Yeah, it looks cool.  I just couldn't drive it.  I'd be embarassed to drive the car, it practically <I>screams</I> 'Please notice the person driving this car.  He is obviously much cooler than you because his car is 100% custom.'  It's like high-quality rice.<P>Sure, it's well done.  It's still rice.<P>I'd rather look a little bit modified, or even bone stock and have a motor under the deck that would make The Tool Man say "Isn't that a bit overboard?"<P>It's the same reason I wouldn't buy an F40 replica.  Looks like it can eat a Porsche for lunch, can't beat your mom's Caprice.  My nearly stock GT would give that 30k (?!) car a run for it's money.<P>It's a silly, silly car.<P>But then that's just my opinion.||||reg||1
